      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "THINK I DO (6) is the one to beat off a clear forgive run at Canterbury, where she was wide without cover for the majority over 1900m and was bumped near the 300m. The return to 1650m suits, with two wins and four placings from six attempts at the distance. The inside draw is a big tick, and she can return to winning ways back in trip. MISS STALWART (5) is racing well without winning and maps to get a lovely chance once again. The 2kg claim gets her right down in the weights now and if she can run up to her recent form, she'll be right in the finish. ONEFORIAN (3) has been beaten at Kembla BM64 company at his past two. Back to country company now is a big tick and Keatings knows him well. Can press on and give them something to catch. RILEYCAT (4) was plain last start at Canterbury, though her previous third there after being held up shows she is capable of improving back in this company. PERUNO (8) is worth keeping safe.",
